nd term in a rematch of her 2022 contest against Republican Christine Drazan. Oregon's Democratic lean and the power of incumbency favor Kotek, and nonpartisan raters mostly call the race Lean Democratic, with several rating it Likely Democratic. Betting markets price her chances around 75 percent.\n\nStill, the contest looks genuinely competitive. The most recent surveys show the two essentially tied, with Drazan slightly ahead in a late-September poll, and coverage has emphasized wrong-track sentiment, public safety, and homelessness. A third-party candidate, Brett Smith, appears on the ballot and could draw votes from either side. The first debate was contentious, with both candidates attacking over donors and records. Kotek holds the edge, but the size of that edge is uncertain.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 7.23}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7143, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6673, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6685, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7762, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7478, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.743, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7131, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7358, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7337, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7182, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7487, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7254, "margin": 3.5}]}